    "problem": "Existing coarse-resolution ocean models yield uncertain estimates of ventilation timescales because their reliance on parameterizing mesoscale eddies, rather than explicitly simulating them, makes it difficult to accurately capture the impact of turbulent, unsteady ocean flows on tracer transport.",
    "method": "This paper proposes a method to estimate the ocean's Transit Time Distribution (TTD) by simulating and averaging an ensemble of Boundary Impulse Response functions (BIRs) in a century-long, high-resolution global ocean model that explicitly resolves mesoscale eddies.",
    "task": "The task is to quantify ocean ventilation timescales and their variability by simulating an ensemble of Boundary Impulse Response functions in a century-long, high-resolution global ocean model that explicitly resolves mesoscale eddies, rather than parameterizing them.",
